{
  "description": "Build a simple reality interface that helps people observe facts, understand context, and make better decisions.",
  "rules": [
    "Start from observable facts. Clearly separate raw observations from hypotheses and conclusions.",
    "Prefer the simplest working solution. Remove unnecessary abstractions, theoretical layers, and unused code.",
    "Keep humans responsible for decisions. Software records, processes, and presents information; it does not infer user intentions or psychological states.",
    "Log only behavior trajectories (e.g., START, CLICK_MAP, FINISH, EXIT). Do not optimize metrics like scroll depth or pause duration as independent indicators of failure.",
    "Design for low cognitive load. Use clear language, explicit assumptions, and simple, non-vibrating interfaces.",
    "Treat deployment as the beginning of validation, not the end. True validation occurs exclusively outside the model, under real-world load in the FIELD.",
    "Before implementing any feature ask: Does this help someone understand reality and make a better decision? If not, don't build it."
  ]
}
